      "entryId": "jud-1-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, the Lord cometh with ten thousands of his saints. Textual proof: Genesis 5:18-24 — Enoch walked with God and was translated; Hebrews 11:5; the prophetic word is second-coming language consistent with Zech 14:5 and 2 Thess 1:7.",
      "density": 2.8,
      "words": 48,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 28,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Genesis 5:18",
          "Hebrews 11:5",
          "Zechariah 14:5",
          "2 Thessalonians 1:7"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "jud-1-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The archangel disputes with the devil but says only, The Lord rebuke thee. First principle: even angelic conflict is conducted in deference — the rebuke belongs to the LORD; Zechariah 3 shows the same scene over Joshua.",
      "density": 2.2964,
      "words": 37,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "jud-1-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Fallen angels reserved in everlasting chains to the great day. First principle: abandonment of station has a reservation — the darkness-chains hold until judgment; the same fate is warned against the false teachers.",
      "density": 2.1393,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "jud-1-24",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The keeping God presents the faultless before glory with joy. First principle: the doxology is soteriology — kept, presented, joyous; the One who saves is the One who finishes.",
      "density": 1.8107,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "jud-1-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The saved-out generation died in the wilderness for unbelief. First principle: past salvation does not immunize against future judgment — the exodus ended at Kadesh for the faithless.",
      "density": 1.7857,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "jud-1-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Three Old Testament rebels map three New Testament sins. First principle: the old rebels are type-men — envy, greed, and usurpation have canonical case studies and one Woe.",
      "density": 1.7857,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "jud-1-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Strange flesh and eternal fire — an example set forth. First principle: the ash-cities are a standing exhibition — eternal fire already visibly burned once as a preview.",
      "density": 1.7286,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
